# AegisAgent — Cursor Project Rules

## Project Overview

AegisAgent is an autonomous AI Red-Team agent that analyzes GitHub Pull Requests
for database vulnerabilities. It competes in three sponsor tracks:
  - Greptile  — diff classification (does this PR touch DB code?)
  - Nia       — WAF bypass intelligence (how do we get past the firewall?)
  - AllScale  — automated bounty payouts (pay out when a vuln is confirmed)

## Core User Flow

```
PR Created
  → Agent fetches diff (github_client)
  → Greptile classifies: DB touched? (greptile_client)
  → If yes: Nia returns WAF bypass strategies (nia_client)
  → sqlmap / nuclei scan the endpoint (tools/)
  → LLM simplifies raw scan output (core/agent.py)
  → AllScale triggers bounty payout (allscale_client)
  → Agent edits the pending PR comment with final results (github_client)
```

## MANDATORY: Read docs/ Before Writing Code

Before editing ANY file in this project, read the relevant guide in docs/:

  - docs/stream_1_brain.md   → core/agent.py, main.py
  - docs/stream_2_muscle.md  → tools/
  - docs/stream_3_context.md → integrations/

These docs define the exact API contracts between streams. Violating them
will cause merge conflicts and break other team members' work.

## File Ownership Map (DO NOT cross streams)

| Stream       | Owner files                  | Must NOT edit               |
|--------------|------------------------------|-----------------------------|
| Brain        | core/agent.py, main.py       | tools/, integrations/       |
| Muscle       | tools/                       | core/, integrations/        |
| Context      | integrations/                | core/, tools/, main.py      |

## Shared State Contract

All data flowing between LangChain/LangGraph nodes must be passed as a
`PRScanState` (Pydantic BaseModel defined in core/agent.py). Never pass
raw dicts between nodes. The full field list is in core/agent.py.

## Key Invariants

1. Every sqlmap/nuclei subprocess MUST use asyncio.wait_for(timeout=60).
   On TimeoutError, return {"status": "timeout", ...} — never raise.

2. The GitHub bot posts ONE comment immediately (post_pending_status) and
   then edits that same comment at the end (update_pr_comment). Never
   post multiple bot comments on a single PR.

3. Use python main.py --mock for all local dev loops. Never hit the live
   GitHub or Greptile API during prompt iteration.
